list.item:
the score is distance − radius × 4096, so a node's radius pulls it closer in the ranking. A
large sloppy node beats a small precise one that is slightly nearer — which is what fixes the radius's
unit as metres;

remarks.code:
time += rate;
if (time >= duration || (backwards && time <= 0)) {
    ended = true;
    if (looping) time += backwards ? duration : -duration;
    else time = backwards ? 0 : duration;
}

